<section class="set-help-list set-about-more" aria-labelledby="set-about-more-h">
    <h3 id="set-about-more-h">More about MetaForge Studio</h3>

    <details>
        <summary>What the licence means for you</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p><strong>You may:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>use MetaForge Studio for any purpose, at home or at work;</li>
                <li>give copies to other people;</li>
                <li>read the code and change it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>If you share a changed version, you must:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>share it under the same licence;</li>
                <li>make its source code available;</li>
                <li>say that you changed it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>You may not</strong> remove the licence or the copyright notices.</p>
            <p class="note">This is a summary to help you. The licence itself is what counts.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>The MetaForge name and logo</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p>The licence covers the code. It does not cover the name "MetaForge Studio" or the MetaForge logo.</p>
            <p>If you share a changed version, give it a different name and logo, so people can tell it apart from this one.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What leaves your computer</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p>Your music files never leave your computer. To find information about them, MetaForge Studio sends small pieces of information to these services, using the keys you entered in Settings.</p>
            <div class="set-about-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="set-about-sent-cap">
                <table>
                    <caption id="set-about-sent-cap">What is sent to each service</caption>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">What is sent</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><th scope="row">MusicBrainz</th><td>Artist, album and track names; your email address</td><td>To identify releases. MusicBrainz asks each user for a contact address.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">AcoustID</th><td>A "fingerprint" of the audio and the track's length. When you submit a track: its title, artist, album and year too.</td><td>To recognise a recording by its sound.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">Discogs</th><td>Artist and album names</td><td>Release years, credits, cover art and artist photos.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">Wikipedia</th><td>Artist and album names</td><td>Release years and credits.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">Google Gemini</th><td>Artist, album and track names, and the questions MetaForge asks about them. No audio is sent.</td><td>Genre, mood, credits, release years and biographies.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">GitHub</th><td>Nothing about you</td><td>To check for a new version.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>Every request names the program as "MetaForgeStudio" with a link to the project page. Only MusicBrainz receives your email address.</p>
            <p>Each service has its own terms and privacy policy. You agree to them when you create your keys.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Programs included with MetaForge Studio</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p>MetaForge Studio runs these programs to do specific jobs. Each is a separate program with its own licence. Choose a licence name to read it.</p>
            <div data-about-table="programs"></div>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Libraries</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p>MetaForge Studio is built on these open-source libraries. Thank you to the people who make them.</p>
            <div data-about-table="libraries"></div>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Fonts and images</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <div data-about-table="fonts"></div>
            <div data-about-table="images"></div>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Where the information comes from</summary>
        <div class="set-help-body">
            <p>MetaForge Studio would be nothing without these services and the people who contribute to them:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>MusicBrainz</strong>, the open music encyclopedia.</li>
                <li><strong>AcoustID</strong>, the open audio fingerprint database.</li>
                <li><strong>Discogs</strong>, the music database and marketplace.</li>
                <li><strong>Wikipedia</strong>, the free encyclopedia. Text from Wikipedia is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike licence.</li>
                <li><strong>Google Gemini</strong>, for AI-assisted suggestions. AI suggestions can be wrong; MetaForge marks where each fact came from.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The names and logos of these services are trademarks of their owners. They are not covered by MetaForge Studio's licence. MetaForge Studio is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by any of them.</p>
            <p>MetaForge Studio uses the Discogs API but is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by Discogs. "Discogs" is a trademark of Zink Media, LLC.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>
<!-- --- END OF FILE about.mfi --- -->
